msgstr ""
"Explain how axis names differ between space group settings and what "
"pseudocubic notation cannot describe."

#: ../../solid/pseudocubic.rst:25
msgid "擬立方胞と各相の胞"
msgstr "Pseudocubic Cell and the Cells of Individual Phases"

#: ../../solid/pseudocubic.rst:27
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"理想的なペロブスカイト型構造ABO\\ :sub:`3`\\ は空間群 :math:`Pm\\bar3m` "
"をとり、単純立方格子の胞に1化学式単位を含む（BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ では胞の一辺が約4 Å）。BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\"
" の正方晶・直方（斜方）晶・菱面体晶の相は、この構造から原子がわずかに変位し、格子が少し歪んだものである [`Kwei 1993 "
"<https://doi.org/10.1021/j100112a043>`__]。空間群の慣用単位胞の軸は相ごとに向きも大きさも異なる。一方、これらの相では原子の変位で並進周期が変わらないので、どの相でも、立方胞の3辺から連続的に変形した3本の格子ベクトルを選べる。この3本を辺とする胞を\\"
" **擬立方胞**\\ （pseudocubic cell）と呼び、格子行列を :math:`A_{\\rm pc}=(\\boldsymbol "
"a_{\\rm pc},\\boldsymbol b_{\\rm pc},\\boldsymbol c_{\\rm pc})` "
"と書く。添字pcを付けた方向・面の指数は、この胞の基底での係数を表す。各相の胞は、\\ :ref:`基底変換<lt-primitive-"
"basis>`\\ の行列 :math:`P` を使って"
msgstr ""
"The ideal perovskite structure ABO\\ :sub:`3` \\ has space group "
":math:`Pm\\bar3m` and contains one formula unit per simple cubic cell "
"(for BaTiO\\ :sub:`3` \\ the cell edge is about 4 Å). The tetragonal, "
"orthorhombic, and rhombohedral phases of BaTiO\\ :sub:`3` \\ arise from "
"small atomic displacements and a slight lattice distortion of this "
"structure [`Kwei 1993 <https://doi.org/10.1021/j100112a043>`__]. The axes"
" of the conventional cells for the space groups differ in orientation and"
" length from phase to phase. However, the atomic displacements in these "
"phases leave the translational periodicity unchanged, so in each phase we"
" can choose three lattice vectors obtained by continuously deforming the "
"three cubic cell edges. We call the cell spanned by these vectors the \\ "
"**pseudocubic cell** \\ and write its lattice matrix as :math:`A_{\\rm "
"pc}=(\\boldsymbol a_{\\rm pc},\\boldsymbol b_{\\rm pc},\\boldsymbol "
"c_{\\rm pc})`. Direction and plane indices with the subscript pc are "
"coefficients in this cell's basis. Using the \\ :ref:`basis "
"transformation <lt-primitive-basis>` \\ matrix :math:`P`, we can write "
"the cell of each phase as"

#: ../../solid/pseudocubic.rst:29
#, python-brace-format
msgid "A=A_{\\rm pc}P,\\qquad V=|\\det P|\\,V_{\\rm pc}"
msgstr "A=A_{\\rm pc}P,\\qquad V=|\\det P|\\,V_{\\rm pc}"

#: ../../solid/pseudocubic.rst:34
msgid ""
"と表せる。:numref:`lt-batio3-pseudocubic-table` "
"に各相の胞と擬立方胞の関係をまとめる。分極の向きの列は、等価な方向の族から1つを選んで書いた。"
msgstr ""
":numref:`lt-batio3-pseudocubic-table` summarizes the relationship between"
" the pseudocubic cell and the cell of each phase. The polarization column"
" lists one representative direction from each family of equivalent "
"directions."

